  "quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "he made an argument last month that voice is the human preferred input for AIs. But that we prefer visuals as the output.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=1s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "The models that we have so far, the experiences that people most people have seen are both slow and dumb, which is like not a great combination.",
      "timestamp_sec": 132,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=132s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "When we're speaking, we have more words per minute than when we're typing. But we also convey more with each word.",
      "timestamp_sec": 192,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=192s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "There's a huge difference in between if you say to me okay versus if you say okay.",
      "timestamp_sec": 192,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=192s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "the voice agent within a second responded that it had done so. And that feels perfectly natural when you get it really dialed in.",
      "timestamp_sec": 256,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=256s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "It doesn't need to be voice. It is just taking action on your intent.",
      "timestamp_sec": 302,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=302s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "there's a huge barrier, a huge challenge to making this actually work and feel good. And that is the tyranny of latency.",
      "timestamp_sec": 302,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=302s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "We we've known since the '60s that to have a computer react to us fast enough that it feels instant, it needs to react in about 100 milliseconds, a tenth of a second.",
      "timestamp_sec": 302,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=302s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "They ask Siri to do something, takes more than a second, we're off to something else mentally, right?",
      "timestamp_sec": 354,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=354s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "We need to have a 200 millisecond latency or less if we want to have a fully conversive people are verbalizing something and they are interrupting or interjecting or agreeing",
      "timestamp_sec": 400,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=400s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "we don't need to wait for novel architectures. We can just switch to having voice in visuals out and then we benefit from the more forgiving visual response envelope that people have.",
      "timestamp_sec": 444,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=444s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "it also has to be on an inference platform that prioritizes latency.",
      "timestamp_sec": 542,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=542s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "in practice we were seeing latencies of 5,000 milliseconds, 7,000 P95, sometimes 10,000 millisecond latency for this small model.",
      "timestamp_sec": 542,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=542s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "Haiku is much better um in terms of of that that P95 latency.",
      "timestamp_sec": 542,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=542s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "if there is a larger chunk of work that needs to get done, then that model then hands off or sends off an asynchronous message to a larger model that can think",
      "timestamp_sec": 591,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=591s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "you're you're blown your budget by a pretty wide margin just for waiting for silence.",
      "timestamp_sec": 634,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=634s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "being willing to send inference every 1 or 2 seconds as they speak",
      "timestamp_sec": 634,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=634s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "if the beginning of the context you send to the model is the same each time, then you can get up to 90% cheaper, faster inference um depending on the conditions.",
      "timestamp_sec": 682,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=682s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    },
    {
      "quote": "we want to the first 90% of the context window if we can to be the same from request to request, and then just use that final 10%",
      "timestamp_sec": 682,
      "talk_slug": "voice-in-visuals-out-the-agony-and-the-ecstasy",
      "deep_link": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=65X0pQ6Lmbg&t=682s",
      "speaker_attributed": true
    }
